      "type": "text",
      "md": "$\\log_a x = y \\iff a^y = x$. Gesetze: $\\log(xy) = \\log x + \\log y$, $\\log\\frac{x}{y} = \\log x - \\log y$, $\\log x^k = k\\log x$, $\\log_a x = \\frac{\\log_b x}{\\log_b a}$. Logarithmen gibt es nur von positiven Zahlen.",
      "id": "t1"
    },
    {
      "type": "choice",
      "md": "What is $\\log_2 48 - \\log_2 3$?",
      "options": [
        {
          "md": "4",
          "correct": true
        },
        {
          "md": "$\\log_2 45$"
        },
        {
          "md": "5"
        },
        {
          "md": "16"
        }
      ],
      "explain": "$\\log_2 \\frac{48}{3} = \\log_2 16 = 4$.",
      "lang": "en",
      "label": "Test question",
      "id": "c1"
    },
